From c74e8fe723294f9fa007fda3d6d6069bebafd5c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Pronyashin <msg@proglyk.ru>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 15:06:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Initial import: owgw-spi-master out-of-tree IIO driver

Out-of-tree IIO driver for the OWGW SPI Master (STM32-based 1-Wire
gateway, up to 16 temperature channels). Targets kernel 4.19 LTS as the
in-house development environment; builds on 5.10/5.15/6.1/6.6/6.12
via the included GitHub Actions CI.

Includes:
  - owgw-spi-master.c                driver source (verbatim from
                                      in-house kernel-firefly branch
                                      larus100rev3, uncommitted as of
                                      2026-08-11)
  - include/linux/iio/temperature/owgw_iface.h
                                      vendored protocol header (verbatim)
  - README.md                        description, build/install/test
  - LICENSE                          GPLv2 (required by MODULE_LICENSE)
  - Makefile                         out-of-tree build (ccflags-y -I$(src))
  - dkms.conf                        DKMS packaging for end users
  - .github/workflows/build.yml      CI matrix over several LTS kernels
  - Documentation/...                Device Tree binding schema
  - patches/                         git format-patch artifacts for
                                      apply-to-tree users, with a
                                      cover-letter.txt
  - .gitignore                       kernel build + agent-specific noise
  - CLAUDE.md                        context for future Claude sessions
  - MEMORY.md                        internal scratchpad
